Looking at this problem, I need to implement a minimax game tree search on a 3×3 grid. The state space is small (3^9 = 19,683 possible board states), so full game tree search with memoization is feasible.

Key observations:
- The board state uniquely determines whose turn it is (count of filled cells % 2) and both players' scores (red cells = Takahashi's, blue cells = Aoki's)
- Game ends immediately on 3-in-a-row, otherwise when board is full the higher score wins
- Sum of all values is odd, guaranteeing no ties when board fills up

